# Every asset filename carries a hash of that file's contents (app.<hash>.css).
# Git's Windows default, core.autocrlf=true, rewrites LF to CRLF on checkout,
# which changes the bytes, which makes every hashed CSS and JS file look
# "edited but not rehashed" on a Windows clone. It cost a deploy on 2026-09-03.
# Disable all text translation: bytes on disk match bytes in the repo, on every
# machine.
* -text
